This project ports content and algorithms from:

  Interactive Low-Poly Environment
  https://github.com/1391819/interactive-low-poly-environment
  Copyright (c) 2022 Roberto Nacu
  License: MIT

The following are derived works (re-authored in TypeScript with module
boundaries; not vendored verbatim):

  - The color palette at js/main.js:181 (lifted as the named-palette extension
    in src/style.ts)
  - Vertex deformation algorithms: getDeformedCylinder, getDeformedBox,
    getFlatIcosahedron, grassDeformation, deformLog (re-authored in
    src/deform.ts as Shape modifier methods)
  - The catalog of object constructors: Stone, Cloud, Sky, AirPlane, Fence,
    LampPost, FireflyColony, Grass, House, Bench, Carousel, Campfire
    (re-authored as catalog/<group>/<slug>.ts modules)
  - Custom GLSL shaders for fire and fireflies (re-authored in src/materials.ts)
  - Day/night light state machine (re-authored in src/world.ts daytime())
  - Texture files water-*.png, flame.png, laketerrain*.png (used directly
    under the MIT terms)

The full upstream source is also vendored verbatim under viewer/upstream/ to
serve as a side-by-side visual reference for our ports. The vendored copy
includes index.html, index.css, js/, textures/, and 5 runtime images
(midday/night/sunrise/sunset SVGs + logo.png). Two paths are patched from
"/textures/foo" to "textures/foo" so they resolve under viewer/upstream/.

The following files from the source repo are NOT included or ported, due to
unverified third-party provenance:

  - obj/Cat.gltf
  - obj/Pug.gltf
  (Two gltfLoader.load() calls in main.js will 404 against the vendored
  copy and log a console error; the rest of the scene renders normally.)

