The contents of `assets/quaternius/` are vendored from Quaternius's free
asset packs (CC0). Quaternius packs are flat-shaded faceted-polygon models
with vertex colors and rigged animations — the canonical "Quaternius style".
Source: GitHub mirror at https://github.com/trebeljahr/quaternius-showcase
(public/glb/), which redistributes the original packs from quaternius.com.

  Creatures (animal-focused):
  - Animals Pack (12 land animals — alpaca, bull, cow, deer, donkey, fox,
    horse, husky, shibainu, stag, wolf, etc.)
  - Cute Fish Pack (52 fish + boat/dock props)
  - Fish Pack (7 additional fish — dolphin, manta ray, shark, whale, etc.)
  - Dinosaurs Pack (6 — apatosaurus, parasaurolophus, stegosaurus, trex,
    triceratops, velociraptor)
  - Easy Enemies Pack (6 critters — frog, rat, snake, spider, wasp)

  Library expansion (16 packs, ~917 GLBs covering nature, buildings,
  characters, weapons, items, furniture, platformer game pieces):
  - Nature Pack (150 — trees, rocks, plants, terrain)
  - Simple Nature Pack (13 — lighter-weight nature primitives)
  - Medieval Village Pack (44 — houses, walls, towers)
  - Modular Medieval Buildings Pack (30 — building parts)
  - Modular Dungeon Pack (41 — dungeon kit)
  - Modular Dungeon 1 (48 — larger dungeon kit)
  - Modular Men (11 — humanoid male characters)
  - Modular Women (10 — humanoid female characters)
  - Single Knight Pack (9 — knight variants)
  - Medieval Weapons Pack (24 — swords, shields, staves)
  - Crops Pack (102 — fruits, vegetables, farming)
  - RPG Items Pack (106 — potions, scrolls, fantasy loot)
  - House Interior Pack (123 — furniture / interior props)
  - Survival Pack (53 — crafting / camping props)
  - Platformer Pack (53 — coins/gems/level blocks)
  - Platformer Game Pack (100 — additional platformer items)

License: CC0 1.0 Universal. Attribution to Quaternius (kindly) appreciated
but not required.

These are simpler/blockier than the KayKit packs above — included as a
lower-detail style option. License: CC0 1.0 Universal.

The file `assets/characters/soldier.glb` is also kept, vendored from the
Three.js example assets at https://threejs.org/examples/models/gltf/Soldier.glb.
This is a Mixamo-rigged photoreal humanoid (Adobe ToS allows redistribution
as part of games/applications). Used as an alternative photoreal asset to
demonstrate the RealisticBody widget works across rig styles.

